<!--
  Kuna: Itanium constructors and destructors named from the vptr stores.
  P1 external-refinement (itaniumrtti); P0 assertion: option itaniumrtti off|on.

  The fixtures are one C++ source built stripped and hidden at -O0 and -O2, so
  only the Itanium RTTI graph names anything. The Listing is on in both passes.

  Asserts #1-#3 are the off pass: on_stack calls Dog's constructor and its
  destructor as bare sub_ names, and the copy constructor is a sub_ storing a
  raw vptr constant. Asserts #4-#7 are the on pass: on_stack calls
  zoo::Dog::Dog and zoo::Dog::~Dog (the destructor replaces its slot-index
  name), and the copy constructor is zoo::Dog::Dog calling zoo::Animal::Animal.
  Asserts #8-#9: Counter has no virtual destructor, so its constructor and its
  destructor, which store the vptr the same way, both stay sub_ in both passes.
  Assert #10: at -O2 make_dog inlines the constructor and stores the vptr
  through operator new's result, not through `this`, so it keeps its name.
-->
<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
